# Everything here is optional. Anything left blank can instead be held in the
# browser under the key button in the top bar — worse, but it works without
# access to this file. The server's value always wins.
#
# Everything here is optional. Without a key, each feature falls back to
# something that still works and says so in the UI.

# The Builder's "Generate" dialog: plan, critique, prompts, finish, ideas,
# ask, build. Without it you copy the blueprint into any agent.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The tweet console: post to X from the app. See docs/X-KEYS.md.
# Without them, Send opens X's compose page with the words.
X_API_KEY=
X_API_SECRET=
X_ACCESS_TOKEN=
X_ACCESS_SECRET=
# X_HANDLE=yourhandle
# X_MEDIA_API=v2

# Publish: push the site (site/document.json, the blueprint, any generated
# code) to a GitHub repository in one commit. A fine-grained token with
# Contents: read and write on that repository.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
GITHUB_REPO=owner/name
# GITHUB_BRANCH=main

# Vercel deploys a connected repository on every push by itself. For a
# project that is not connected, paste its deploy hook URL and Publish calls
# it after the push.
# VERCEL_DEPLOY_HOOK=https://api.vercel.com/v1/integrations/deploy/…

# Screenshots and tour recordings on the server need Playwright. It is found
# in the project, at this path, or in the usual global places.
# PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=/opt/node22/lib/node_modules/playwright
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM=/path/to/chromium
# FFMPEG=/path/to/ffmpeg
